# Source language of this project's checkout, read by
# tools/check_comment_only_streams.sh to pick the comment-only prover.
#
# GZDoom is C++, but its comment syntax (// and /* */) is identical to C, and
# the shared C prover (tools/prove_comment_only.sh) already globs *.cpp/*.hpp/
# *.cc and strips comments with `gcc -xc -fpreprocessed -dD -E -P`. C mode
# tokenizes these files cleanly (verified: exit 0, comments removed) and, since
# any C++-specific token is handled identically on both the before/after sides,
# the strip-then-compare proof holds. The dispatcher only knows c/rust/kotlin
# (a `cpp` value would be rejected), so declare `c` and reuse the C prover
# rather than extending the shared stripper.
c
